PHONE

TITLE
Java to C Converter, with Support for Ptolemy II SDF Actors

CHAPTER
02.cad

ABSTRACT 
The synchronous dataflow domain of Ptolemy II is excellent for representing 
signal processing systems. This is expressed in Java using the Ptolemy II
models. For the compilation of these models towards existing DSPs Java is
often not directly suited, as there are few Java compilers and 
Java virtual machines for DSP's. The final performance of the total system
might also be hindered by a start with Java at this point in time.

DSP's do have C compilers, which frequently generate optimized code. So
the goal of the project is to generate C code from a Ptolemy II SDF system.
To reach that goal, we must have the ability to translate ordinary Java code 
into C code, which would be useful to many Java programmers. Once
we have that ability, we will optimize the communication between SDF actors,
to produce C code that is reasonably efficient.  

